    {
     "kind": "debate",
     "text": "The phrase is עֵ֖זֶר כְּנֶגְדּֽוֹ. English versions differ: \"helper comparable to him\", \"a help like unto himself\", \"an help meet for him\", \"a help suitable to him\". The Septuagint has βοηθὸν κατ’ αὐτόν; the Vulgate adjutorium simile sibi. How much the word for \"helper\" implies rank, and in which direction, is debated.",
