    {
     "kind": "debate",
     "text": "Who crushes the serpent's head? The Hebrew pronoun ה֚וּא is pronoun, personal, third person, masculine, singular, agreeing with \"offspring\". The Septuagint has the masculine αὐτός. The Clementine Vulgate reads the feminine ipsa, and the Douay-Rheims follows it: \"she shall crush thy head\". The King James has \"it shall bruise thy head\". Each reading points to a different subject: the offspring, a descendant, or the woman.",
     "sources": []
    }
